### 1) Register a fresh user (also creates an EmailVerificationRequested event)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Verify Me", "email": "verify1@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

### 2) Login
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }

> {% client.global.set("vtoken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3) emailVerified must be false
GET http://localhost:5001/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}

### 4) Request a new code right away (expect 429 - cooldown)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/request
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}

### 5) Without token (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/request

### 6) Wrong code (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "000000" }

### 7) Bad format (expect 400 with errors)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "12ab" }

### 8) Correct code from the SQL query (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "PASTE_CODE_HERE" }

### 9) emailVerified must be true now
GET http://localhost:5001/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}

### 10) Request again (expect 409 - already verified)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/verify-email/request
Authorization: Bearer {{vtoken}}

### 11) Forgot password - existing email (expect 202)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com" }

### 12) Forgot password - unknown email (expect 202 with the SAME body)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com" }

### 13) Reset with a wrong code (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "code": "000000", "newPassword": "BrandNewPass789" }

### 14) Weak new password (expect 400 with errors)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "code": "123456", "newPassword": "short" }

### 15) Reset with the correct code from the SQL query (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "code": "PASTE_CODE_HERE", "newPassword": "BrandNewPass789" }

### 16) Reuse the same code (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "code": "PASTE_CODE_HERE", "newPassword": "AnotherPass123" }

### 17) Login with the new password (expect 200)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "password": "BrandNewPass789" }

### 18) Login with the old password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "verify1@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd123" }